# 19_shamanic_journey_RGB.ledc — Shamanic Journey (Theta Drum), RGB inner/outer build
# RGB variant of 19_shamanic_journey. Audio + speech IDENTICAL (isochronic ~4.5 Hz drum,
# descent -> journey -> callback -> wake). LEDs on inner ring (mask 9, warm amber
# 255,160,32) + outer ring (mask 6, deep amber 255,80,0), 180 antiphase, SQUARE gate
# (the sharp drum pulse) — the inner<->outer alternation is a radial drumbeat. Warm amber
# (NON-saturated, safe to flicker); every rate <=10 Hz; brightness <=30%. See base header.
#
# LED: time freq duty bright R G B mask [env phase]   (env 0 = square, sharp drum)

# --- Settle (drum 8 Hz): warm amber, vol + light fade in ---
0 8 50 >0 255 160 32 9 0 0       # inner amber: 8 Hz square, fade-in
0 8 50 >0 255 80 0 6 0 180       # outer deep-amber: antiphase (radial drum)
A 0 160 0 >0 8 1                 # ch1 isochronic drum: 160 Hz pulsed at 8 Hz; vol fade-in
S 5000 default 65 "Find a comfortable place to lie down. Let the drum find its rhythm around you."
20000 8 50 22 255 160 32 9 0 0   # inner: 22% reached
20000 8 50 22 255 80 0 6 0 180   # outer
45000 8 50 ~12:30:12000 255 160 32 9 0 0   # inner: breathing 12<->30%
45000 8 50 ~12:30:12000 255 80 0 6 0 180   # outer
A 45000 160 0 50 8 1             # vol settled 50; drum 8 Hz

# --- Descent to drumming theta (pulse 8->4.5, ~0.7 Hz/min) ---
A 180000 160 0 50 >8 1           # isochronic pulse 8 -> 4.5
180000 >8 50 ~12:30:12000 255 160 32 9 0 0   # inner: flicker 8->4.5, breathing
180000 >8 50 ~12:30:12000 255 80 0 6 0 180   # outer
S 180000 default 65 "Let the drum carry you downward, into the journey."

# --- Journey hold (pulse 4.5 Hz): the monotonous shamanic drum ---
A 480000 160 0 55 4.5 1          # steady 4.5 Hz isochronic drum; fuller vol
480000 4.5 50 ~12:30:12000 255 160 32 9 0 0   # inner: 4.5 Hz square, breathing
480000 4.5 50 ~12:30:12000 255 80 0 6 0 180   # outer
S 480000 default 65 "You are in the between-place now. Let the steady drum hold you. Explore."
S 960000 default 65 "Wander freely. The drum is your thread home; it will not let you lose your way."

# --- Callback: faster recall (pulse 4.5->9) ---
A 1320000 160 0 55 >4.5 1        # CALLBACK: isochronic pulse 4.5 -> 9, the recall
1320000 >4.5 50 22 255 160 32 9 0 0   # inner: 4.5->9; steady 22% for the alerting callback
1320000 >4.5 50 22 255 80 0 6 0 180   # outer
S 1320000 default 65 "The drum is calling you back. Begin to return, following the quickening beat."

# --- Gentle wake (pulse 9->10) + soft fade ---
A 1560000 160 0 >55 >9 1         # pulse 9->10; vol eases 55->0 over the wake
1560000 >9 50 >22 255 160 32 9 0 0   # inner: 9->10; bright 22->0
1560000 >9 50 >22 255 80 0 6 0 180   # outer
S 1560000 default 65 "Come fully back to the room. Feel the ground beneath you, and open your eyes when ready."
A 1800000 160 0 0 10 1           # volume 0, pulse settled 10 Hz
1800000 10 50 0 255 160 32 9 0 0     # inner off
1800000 10 50 0 255 80 0 6 0 180     # outer off
